    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542-a1">

                <pb facs="0911" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg841"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    219.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Aarifi Pasha to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Envoy</hi>: The tariff of customs concluded
                    between the Sublime Porte and the Government of the United States of America
                    having ceased to have a legal force since the 13th of March last, the imperial
                    Government has decided to collect hereafter the dues of 8 per cent, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad valorem</hi> on the goods imported in Turkey until a
                    new arrangement takes place.</p>
                <p>As this measure is to be put into execution immediately in all the custom-houses
                    of the Empire, the competent administration has received the necessary orders
                    accordingly.</p>
                <p>In bringing this decision to the knowledge of your excellency, I beg you to
                    accept, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. AARIFI.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
